<% content_for :title, "Archived stocks preview" %>
<%# A design preview, reachable only where the component gallery is - `Rails.env.local?`.

    The question: "if the trading floor paginates, is there value in displaying the archived stocks that
    were removed?" This page renders the two answers side by side, because the argument is easier to have
    against a rendering. %>
<div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
  <%= admin_breadcrumbs(@breadcrumbs) %>

  <%= render layout: "components/ui/page_header",
             locals: { title: "Archived stocks preview",
                       description: "Two treatments of the same rows, to answer whether pagination " \
                                    "changes the case for listing archived companies again." } do %><% end %>

  <div class="space-y-6">
    <%= render layout: "components/ui/callout",
               locals: { tone: :info,
                         title: "The recommendation is B - leave it as it is",
                         body: "Pagination solves a length problem. The archived list was removed for a " \
                               "different reason: no reader could act on it. A student cannot buy an " \
                               "archived company, and a teacher who wants the catalogue has " \
                               "/admin/stocks, which carries more. Making an unusable list shorter does " \
                               "not make it useful." } do %><% end %>

    <section aria-labelledby="option-a">
      <h2 id="option-a" class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">Option A - list them for everyone</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">
        What the trading floor showed before, now paginated. Every archived company inside the retention
        window, to every reader.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-3">
        <% if @archived.any? %>
          <%= render "stocks/stocks_table",
                     title: "Archived stocks",
                     description: "These companies are no longer listed. You cannot buy them.",
                     stocks: @archived %>
        <% else %>
          <%= render "components/ui/empty_state",
                     icon: "chart-line",
                     title: "No stocks in this database",
                     body: "Seed some stocks and this preview renders them." %>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 text-sm text-slate-700">
        <p class="font-medium text-slate-900">What this costs</p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
          <li>Every row carries an action column with nothing in it, for every reader but a holder.</li>
          <li>It doubles the page&rsquo;s tables, so &ldquo;Active stocks&rdquo; is no longer the page.</li>
          <li>A student scanning for something to buy reads a second list they cannot buy from.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="option-b">
      <h2 id="option-b" class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">
        Option B - only what the reader can act on (today)
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">
        The section renders only when the student holds one of them, and the one action it supports is
        Sell.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-3">
        <% if @archived.any? %>
          <%= render "stocks/stocks_table",
                     title: "Archived stocks you hold",
                     description: "You still own shares in these. They cannot be bought any more, " \
                                  "but you can sell whenever you like.",
                     stocks: @archived.first(2) %>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 text-sm text-slate-700">
        <p class="font-medium text-slate-900">What this gives</p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
          <li>Nothing renders for the reader with nothing to sell, which is nearly every reader.</li>
          <li>Every row shown has exactly one thing to do with it.</li>
          <li>The catalogue still exists for staff, at <code>/admin/stocks</code>, with more columns.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
